 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 509940,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>Explain the error in the following calculation, and correct the error:</p>\n<span data-math=\"{149_{14}} + {19_{14}} = {168_{14}}\">{149_{14}} + {19_{14}} = {168_{14}}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The answer is wrong because it shows the answer in base 10 but has a base indicated as base 14. In base 14,</p>\n<p>A represents the digit 10.</p>\n<p>B represents the digit 11.</p>\n<p>C represents the digit 12.</p>\n<p>D represents the digit 13.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Do the one’s place first.</p>\n<p>In base 10: 9 + 9 = 18 = 14 + 4</p>\n<p>In base 14: 14</p>\n<p>One’s place: 4</p>\n<p>Carry: 1</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Carry:</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>+</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>=</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Next step: Do the next place to the left.</p>\n<p>In base 10: 1 + 4 + 1 = 6</p>\n<p>In base 14: 6</p>\n<p>This column: 6</p>\n<p>Carry: No need</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Carry:</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>+</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>=</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Next step: Do the next place to the left.</p>\n<p>In base 10: Bring down the 1.</p>\n<p>In base 14: Bring down the 1.</p>\n<p>This column: 1</p>\n<p>Carry: You don’t need to carry because there are no more columns.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Carry:</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>+</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>=</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"{164_{14}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "This is correct if the numbers are base 10 numbers, but these numbers are base 14 numbers. In base 14, 9 + 9 is not 18, but instead is 13. Careful use of the base 14 addition table generates the correct answer, <span data-math=\"{163_{14}}\">{163_{14}}</span>."
    }
